# Copy to .env.local (local override) or set in your host's BUILD environment.
#
# Origin of the FastAPI backend. Vite inlines VITE_* variables at build time,
# so this must be present when `npm run build` runs — a runtime env var on a
# static host does nothing.
#
# No trailing slash. No /api suffix: the backend serves routes at the root
# (/health, /projects, /runs/...). In dev this is left unset so requests hit
# /api on the same origin and vite.config.ts proxies them.
#
# VITE_API_BASE=https://audience-zero.onrender.com

# The backend must also allow this frontend's origin, or the browser blocks
# every request. On the backend host set (JSON array — a comma-separated list
# raises SettingsError and the app will not start):
#
# AZ_CORS_ORIGINS=["https://audience-zero.netlify.app"]
#
# The origin is scheme://host with NO trailing slash and no path — CORS matches
# it exactly, so "https://audience-zero.netlify.app/" will not match.
